For \(t = 0\), the form of the string will be \[y = A_1 \,.\, \sin\frac{\pi x}{l} + A_2 \,.\, \frac{\sin 2\pi x}{l} + A_3 \,.\, \sin\frac{3\pi x}{l} + \&c. \tag{1c}\] and the velocity of the string will be ¶ \[\frac{dy}{dt} = 2\pi n \left(B_1 \,.\, \sin\frac{\pi x}{l} + 2B_2@@A@@
>>>
<<<
@@A@@
===
 \,.\, \sin\frac{2\pi x}{l} + 3B_3 \,.\, \sin\frac{3\pi x}{l} + \&c.\right) \tag{1d}\]

Now suppose the string to have been drawn aside by a sharp point, and that the point was withdrawn at the time \(t = 0\), so that the vibration commenced at that moment, then for \(t = 0\)@@A@@
>>>
<<<
@@A@@
===
 there was no velocity, that is \(\frac{dy}{dt}\) was \(= 0\) for all values of \(x\). This can only be the case when in equation (1d), \(0 = B_1 = B_2 = B_3 = \&c.\)
@@A@@
