The coefficients \(A_1, A_2, A_3\), &c., depend on the shape of the string at the time \(t = 0\). At the moment the sharp point quitted it the string must have assumed the position of fig. 18 A (p. 54a), that is, it must have formed two straight lines proceeding from the sharp@@A@@
>>>
<<<
@@A@@
===
 point to the fixed extremities of the string. Supposing the position of the sharp point at that moment to be determined by \(x = a\) and \(y = b\), then for the time \(t = 0\), the value of \(y\), was \[y = \frac{bx}{a} \text{ if } a > x > 0 \tag{2}\] ¶ \[\text{and } y = b@@A@@
>>>
