===

To find the coefficient \(A_m\), the well-known method is to multiply both sides of the equation (1c) by \(\sin\frac{m\pi x}{l} \,.\, dx\), and to integrate between the limits \(x = 0\) and \(x = l\). In this case equation (1c) reduces to \[\int_0^l y \,.\, \sin\frac{m\pi x}{l}@@A@@
>>>
<<<
@@A@@
===
 \,.\, dx = A_m \,.\, \int_0^l \sin^2\frac{m\pi x}{l} \,.\, dx \tag{2b}\] in which \(y\) must be replaced by its values in (2) and (2a). Performing the integrations indicated in (2b) we find \[A_m = \frac{2bl^2}{m^2\pi^2 a(l - a)} \,.\, \sin\frac{m\pi a}{l} \tag{3}\]
>>>
